#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""run-tests: run the plugin's pytest suite under a machine-wide suite lock.

The wrapper caps heavy test processes on one machine: at most 2 run at once, and only one full
suite. Run pytest through it, never bare, when several agents or worktrees share a machine.

  run-tests [options]                            QUICK (the default): only the tests that import or
                                                 name what changed since the merge base with main,
                                                 plus a small smoke list; holds ONE worker slot
  run-tests [options] [--] [pytest args...]      targeted run: holds ONE worker slot
  run-tests --full [options]                     full suite: holds the suite slot + one worker slot
  run-tests --raw [options] -- <cmd> [args...]   any other heavy command under one worker slot
  run-tests --status                             who holds which slot, and the suite queue order

Slots, in the lock dir (machine-wide, never HOME or a per-session TMPDIR, since agents may run
with a scratch HOME and their own TMPDIR): /private/tmp on macOS, /tmp elsewhere, else the
system temp dir; REPACTED_LOCK_DIR overrides it.
  <lock dir>/repacted-suite.lock       taken only by --full
  <lock dir>/repacted-worker-1.lock    one of the two is taken by every run
  <lock dir>/repacted-worker-2.lock
Each slot is a flock on the file (on macOS the same lock /usr/bin/lockf takes, so
`lockf -k /private/tmp/repacted-suite.lock <cmd>` and this wrapper exclude each other).
The holder writes `<lock>.owner` (package, pid, start, branch) for `--status`; the lock file,
not the sidecar, is the truth. Never read process command lines to find a holder.

The suite slot is granted in arrival order. Each --full waiter writes a numbered ticket in
<lock dir>/repacted-suite.queue/ and may try the flock only while its ticket is the lowest
LIVE one; it keeps the ticket until it releases the slot. A ticket is live while its pid exists
with the start time it recorded (`ps -o pid=,lstart=`, never a command line), so a dead or
reused-pid holder or waiter is reaped and never blocks the queue. The flock still decides
exclusion: tickets only order the waiters. A copy of this script from before the queue ignores
tickets and just polls the flock, so it can take the slot out of turn but cannot deadlock the
queue (the head waiter keeps polling a flock that copy releases as before).

--full with no pytest args is the merge gate: it runs the plugin suite through tcount and reads
the verdict against the versioned baseline scripts/known-failures.txt:
'gate passed (N known)' only when each suite's failing ids EQUAL its listed ids; a new failure,
a listed id that now passes or is gone (drift), a failure list tcount truncated, or a missing
baseline fails the gate. A narrowed `--full <args>` says on stderr that it is not the merge gate.
Every --full run also gives pytest `--durations=0 --durations-min=0.1`, so tcount's log holds the
wall of each test phase over 0.1 s; after the counts lines the 10 slowest test files are printed
(those phases summed per file), and the suite's row copied to the live ledger carries them as
`slowest: [[file, seconds], ...]`.
Every suite is given REPACT_PURITY_DENYLIST_DIR, the directory of the scrub denylists
(~/.config/repacted of the account's home, never $HOME), which the core purity gate reads;
without a denylist there, that gate fails closed (DENYLIST_REQUIRED), or else is told to run
without one.

The test process runs:
  - from pact-plugin (the canonical `cd pact-plugin && python -m pytest` cwd);
  - with CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR and CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT unset, PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 and a scratch
    HOME (a fresh temp dir unless --home is given), so no run reads or writes the live ~/.claude;
  - with PYTHONUSERBASE kept if set, else the interpreter's user base under the account's home:
    a pytest installed with `pip install --user` is not found under the scratch HOME without it;
    likewise HF_HOME, else the account's huggingface cache, where the embedding model lives;
  - with CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA kept if set, else $TMPDIR/repacted-test-runs, so nothing the suite
    writes lands in the live data dir. Inside a Claude Code session tcount's log goes to the
    live runs/ directory, beside the run ledger that names it (TCOUNT_LOG_DIR); outside one it
    stays under $TMPDIR/repacted-test-runs. This wrapper then copies each suite's tcount row
    into the caller's live run ledger (the child never writes it), where the run-ledger hook
    attributes it by its log path;
  - under `nice -n 19`, through tcount, so the counts line is verifiable (D7);
  - with pytest `-q -p no:cacheprovider`. xdist `-n` is refused: the slot IS the parallelism cap.

Options
  (no args)         QUICK: the changed files are `git diff --name-only <merge-base main>` plus
                    uncommitted and untracked files. A changed test file is selected; any other
                    changed file selects every test file (plugin tests/, skills/*/test_*.py
                    ) that names it (its file name, or `import <stem>` /
                    `from ... import <stem>`). SMOKE is always added. The selection is printed.
                    Use --full for a release or the lead's final merge check.
  --full            take the suite slot too; with no pytest args, collects the whole plugin
                    (tests/ and skills/*/test_*.py)
                    ; with pytest args, runs only those, in the plugin
  --pkg NAME        package name for the owner sidecar (default: the git branch)
  --home DIR        scratch HOME to use (kept); default: a temp dir, removed afterwards
  --python PATH     interpreter with pytest installed (default: $REPACTED_PYTHON, else .venv/bin/python3
                    in this tree or its main checkout, else python3; the choice is printed)
  --wait SECONDS    how long to wait for a slot (default 3600)

Environment
  REPACTED_LOCK_DIR   overrides the lock dir, for the slots and the queue
  REPACTED_PYTHON     default interpreter
  REPACTED_KNOWN_FAILURES, REPACTED_DENYLIST_DIR   override the baseline file and the denylist
                      directory (tests of this wrapper only)

Exit codes
  75  a slot was not acquired within --wait: report it, never bypass the lock
  64  usage error
  *   otherwise tcount's exit code (0 pass, 1 failures, 3 no count parsed); for the merge
      gate, 0 when the verdict passes against the baseline, else the first non-zero code (1)

Examples
  python3 scripts/run-tests -- tests/contract
  python3 scripts/run-tests --full --pkg w0-infra
  python3 scripts/run-tests --status
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import errno
import fcntl
import json
import os
import pwd
import re
import shutil
import signal
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import time
from pathlib import Path

EXIT_USAGE, EXIT_LOCK_TIMEOUT = 64, 75
DEFAULT_LOCK_DIR = "/private/tmp"     # macOS: the real /tmp, shared by every session
SUITE_LOCK = "repacted-suite.lock"
WORKER_LOCKS = ("repacted-worker-1.lock", "repacted-worker-2.lock")
SUITE_QUEUE = "repacted-suite.queue"
POLL_SECONDS = 2.0
HEAD_POLL_SECONDS = 0.2  # the head waiter polls faster, so it usually beats a pre-queue copy
PS = "/bin/ps" if Path("/bin/ps").exists() else "ps"
XDIST_FLAGS = ("-n", "--numprocesses", "--dist")

REPACTED = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent
PLUGIN = REPACTED / "pact-plugin"
REPO = REPACTED
TCOUNT = PLUGIN / "bin" / "tcount"
SMOKE = ("tests/contract", "tests/test_hooks_json.py", "tests/test_path_setup_pin.py")   # contract: budgets, rule homes
VENV_PYTHON = Path(".venv") / "bin" / "python3"
COUNTS_PREFIX = "pytest: collected "
COUNTS_LINE = re.compile(r"^pytest: collected (\d+) · passed \d+ · failed (\d+) · errors (\d+) ")
KNOWN_FAILURES = REPACTED / "scripts" / "known-failures.txt"
SUITES = ("plugin",)
DENYLISTS = ("scrub-denylist.txt", "scrub-denylist-words.txt")
# True: the purity gate is always pointed at the denylist directory and fails closed without one.
# False: with no denylist there, the gate is told to run without one (REPACT_PURITY_NO_DENYLIST).
DENYLIST_REQUIRED = False
SESSION_ENV = "CLAUDE_CODE_SESSION_ID"      # set in every Bash call of a Claude Code session
LOG_DIR_ENV = "TCOUNT_LOG_DIR"
# --full: each test phase over 0.1 s goes into tcount's log, and the slowest files are summed from it
# (pytest's own top-N ranks phases, not files).
DURATIONS = ("--durations=0", "--durations-min=0.1")
SLOWEST_HEADER = re.compile(r"^=+ slowest (?:\d+ )?durations =+$")
DURATION_LINE = re.compile(r"^(\d+(?:\.\d+)?)s +(?:setup|call|teardown) +(\S.*)$")
SLOWEST_FILES = 10


class Usage(Exception):
    pass


def lock_dir() -> Path:
    """REPACTED_LOCK_DIR, else /private/tmp (macOS), /tmp, or the system temp dir: the first that
    is a directory. Never derived from TMPDIR first: a per-session TMPDIR would split the lock."""
    override = os.environ.get("REPACTED_LOCK_DIR")
    if override:
        return Path(override)
    for candidate in (DEFAULT_LOCK_DIR, "/tmp"):
        if os.path.isdir(candidate):
            return Path(candidate)
    return Path(tempfile.gettempdir())


def try_lock(path: Path) -> int | None:
    """An open fd holding an exclusive flock on path, or None if another process holds it."""
    fd = os.open(path, os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o666)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError as exc:
        os.close(fd)
        if exc.errno in (errno.EWOULDBLOCK, errno.EAGAIN):
            return None
        raise
    return fd


def acquire(paths: tuple[Path, ...], deadline: float) -> tuple[int, Path] | None:
    """Wait for the first free lock among paths until deadline. None on timeout."""
    while True:
        for path in paths:
            fd = try_lock(path)
            if fd is not None:
                return fd, path
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            return None
        time.sleep(POLL_SECONDS)


def queue_dir() -> Path:
    return lock_dir() / SUITE_QUEUE


def process_start(pid: int) -> str | None:
    """The start time of pid as ps prints it, or None when no such process exists. Reads no
    command line. LC_ALL and TZ are pinned so every waiter formats the same process identically."""
    env = {"PATH": "/bin:/usr/bin", "LC_ALL": "C", "TZ": "UTC"}
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([PS, "-o", "pid=,lstart=", "-p", str(pid)], capture_output=True,
                             text=True, timeout=10, env=env).stdout.split(None, 1)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        # ps unusable: fall back to existence only, and never reap a process that may be alive.
        try:
            os.kill(pid, 0)
        except ProcessLookupError:
            return None
        except PermissionError:
            pass
        return "?"
    if len(out) != 2 or out[0] != str(pid):
        return None
    return " ".join(out[1].split())


def is_live(ticket: dict) -> bool:
    start = process_start(ticket["pid"])
    return start is not None and (start == "?" or start == ticket["lstart"])


def write_ticket(path: Path, ticket: dict) -> None:
    # Written aside and renamed in, so a reader never sees a half-written ticket.
    tmp = path.with_name(f".{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.tmp")
    tmp.write_text(json.dumps(ticket), encoding="utf-8")
    os.replace(tmp, path)


def read_tickets() -> list[tuple[Path, dict | None]]:
    """Every ticket in arrival order; None for one that does not parse."""
    found = []
    for path in sorted(queue_dir().glob("*.ticket")):
        try:
            found.append((path, json.loads(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8"))))
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            found.append((path, None))
    return found


def take_ticket(pkg: str) -> tuple[Path, dict]:
    """Append this process to the suite queue. The sequence counter lives in `.seq`, under its own
    flock held only for the increment; it never goes below an existing ticket, so a lost counter
    cannot let a newcomer cut in."""
    queue = queue_dir()
    queue.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    fd = os.open(queue / ".seq", os.O_RDWR | os.O_CREAT, 0o666)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(fd, fcntl.LOCK_EX)
        raw_seq = os.read(fd, 64).decode("ascii", "replace").strip()
        last = int(raw_seq) if raw_seq.isdigit() else 0
        for path, _ in read_tickets():
            if path.stem.isdigit():
                last = max(last, int(path.stem))
        seq = last + 1
        os.lseek(fd, 0, os.SEEK_SET)
        os.ftruncate(fd, 0)
        os.write(fd, str(seq).encode("ascii"))
        ticket = {"seq": seq, "pid": os.getpid(), "lstart": process_start(os.getpid()) or "?",
                  "pkg": pkg, "since": time.strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ", time.gmtime())}
        path = queue / f"{seq:012d}.ticket"
        write_ticket(path, ticket)
    finally:
        os.close(fd)
    return path, ticket


def head_of_queue(own: Path, ticket: dict) -> bool:
    """True when own is the lowest live ticket. Reaps dead and unreadable tickets on the way, and
    restores own if another waiter reaped it by mistake, so no process loses its place."""
    if not own.exists():
        write_ticket(own, ticket)
    for path, other in read_tickets():
        if path == own:
            return True
        if other is None or not is_live(other):
            try:
                path.unlink()
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass
            continue
        return False
    return False


def acquire_suite(pkg: str, deadline: float) -> tuple[int, Path, Path] | None:
    """Queue for the suite slot and take its flock in turn. Returns (fd, lock, ticket); the caller
    removes the ticket when it releases the slot. None on timeout, with the ticket already gone."""
    lock = lock_dir() / SUITE_LOCK
    own, ticket = take_ticket(pkg)
    granted = False
    try:
        while True:
            poll = POLL_SECONDS
            if head_of_queue(own, ticket):
                fd = try_lock(lock)
                if fd is not None:
                    granted = True
                    return fd, lock, own
                poll = HEAD_POLL_SECONDS
            remaining = deadline - time.monotonic()
            if remaining <= 0:
                return None
            time.sleep(min(poll, remaining))
    finally:
        if not granted:
            try:
                own.unlink()
            except FileNotFoundError:
                pass


def owner_line(pkg: str) -> str:
    return f"pkg={pkg} pid={os.getpid()} since={time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ', time.gmtime())}\n"


def write_owner(lock: Path, pkg: str) -> Path:
    sidecar = lock.with_name(lock.name + ".owner")
    sidecar.write_text(owner_line(pkg), encoding="utf-8")
    return sidecar


def current_branch() -> str:
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(REPACTED), "branch", "--show-current"],
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
        return out.stdout.strip() or "detached"
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return "unknown"


def status() -> int:
    for name in (SUITE_LOCK, *WORKER_LOCKS):
        path = lock_dir() / name
        fd = try_lock(path)
        if fd is None:
            sidecar = path.with_name(name + ".owner")
            who = sidecar.read_text(encoding="utf-8").strip() if sidecar.exists() else "no sidecar"
            print(f"{name}: HELD ({who})")
        else:
            os.close(fd)
            print(f"{name}: free")
    tickets = read_tickets() if queue_dir().is_dir() else []
    print(f"suite queue: {len(tickets) or 'empty'}")
    for n, (path, ticket) in enumerate(tickets, 1):
        if ticket is None:
            print(f"  {n}. {path.name}: unreadable")
            continue
        state = "live" if is_live(ticket) else "dead"
        print(f"  {n}. pkg={ticket['pkg']} pid={ticket['pid']} since={ticket['since']} ({state})")
    return 0


def build_steps(args, pytest_args: list[str]) -> list[tuple[str, list[str], Path]]:
    """(label, command, cwd) for each suite to run, in order."""
    if args.raw:
        if not pytest_args:
            raise Usage("--raw needs a command after --")
        return [("raw", ["nice", "-n", "19", *pytest_args], PLUGIN)]
    for arg in pytest_args:
        if arg.split("=", 1)[0] in XDIST_FLAGS or (arg.startswith("-n") and arg[2:].isdigit()):
            raise Usage(f"refused: {arg!r}. The worker slot is the parallelism cap (D11); run without xdist")
    python = default_python(args.python)
    print(f"run-tests: interpreter {shutil.which(python) or python}", file=sys.stderr)

    def pytest(*extra: str) -> list[str]:
        return ["nice", "-n", "19", python, str(TCOUNT), "--", python, "-m", "pytest",
                *(DURATIONS if args.full else ()), "-q", "-p", "no:cacheprovider", *extra]

    if pytest_args:
        return [("plugin", pytest(*pytest_args), PLUGIN)]
    if not args.full:
        plugin_tests, picked = quick_selection(changed_files())
        steps = [("plugin", pytest(*plugin_tests), PLUGIN)]
        counts, listed = f"{len(plugin_tests)} plugin", list(plugin_tests)
        print(f"run-tests: QUICK: {counts} test file(s) (--full runs everything)", file=sys.stderr)
        for name in listed:
            print(f"  {name}", file=sys.stderr)
        return steps
    # --full with no args is the merge gate: the whole plugin (tests/ AND the skills/*/test_*.py
    # modules).
    steps = [("plugin", pytest(), PLUGIN)]
    return steps


def _git(*args: str) -> list[str]:
    run = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(REPO), *args], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    return [line for line in run.stdout.splitlines() if line.strip()] if run.returncode == 0 else []


def changed_files() -> list[str]:
    """Repo-relative paths changed since the merge base with main, plus uncommitted and untracked."""
    base = _git("merge-base", "HEAD", "main")
    names = set(_git("diff", "--name-only", base[0])) if base else set()
    names |= set(_git("diff", "--name-only", "HEAD")) | set(_git("ls-files", "--others", "--exclude-standard"))
    return sorted(names)


def _test_files() -> list[Path]:
    """Every test file a QUICK run may select. tests/slow/ (worst-case timings) is left to
    --full, whose bare collection reaches it; QUICK never times a regex on a shared laptop."""
    slow = PLUGIN / "tests" / "slow"
    found = {*(p for p in (PLUGIN / "tests").rglob("test_*.py") if slow not in p.parents),
             *(PLUGIN / "skills").glob("*/test_*.py")}
    return sorted(found)


def quick_selection(changed: list[str]) -> tuple[list[str], list[str]]:
    """(plugin-relative, repo-relative) test files for a QUICK run: changed tests, tests that name
    a changed file, and SMOKE."""
    tests = _test_files()
    chosen: set[Path] = set()
    for rel in changed:
        path = REPO / rel
        if path in tests:
            chosen.add(path)
            continue
        stem = Path(rel).stem
        if not stem or path.suffix not in ("", ".py", ".sh", ".md", ".json"):
            continue
        pattern = re.compile(rf"(?:{re.escape(Path(rel).name)}\b|import {re.escape(stem)}\b|"
                             rf"from [\w.]+ import [^\n]*\b{re.escape(stem)}\b)")
        for test in tests:
            try:
                if pattern.search(test.read_text(encoding="utf-8", errors="replace")):
                    chosen.add(test)
            except OSError:
                continue
    chosen |= {PLUGIN / name for name in SMOKE if (PLUGIN / name).exists()}
    plugin = sorted(str(p.relative_to(PLUGIN)) for p in chosen if PLUGIN in p.parents)
    root = sorted(str(p.relative_to(REPO)) for p in chosen if PLUGIN not in p.parents)
    return plugin, root


def main_checkout() -> Path | None:
    """The main checkout this tree belongs to (itself, outside a worktree), or None."""
    try:
        out = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(REPO), "rev-parse", "--path-format=absolute",
                              "--git-common-dir"], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=10)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    common = out.stdout.strip()
    return Path(common).parent if not out.returncode and common else None




def default_python(given: str | None = None) -> str:
    """ONE interpreter for every builder: --python, else $REPACTED_PYTHON, else the
    venv of this tree or of its main checkout, else python3 from PATH. A bare python3 differs between
    builders' PATHs, which is how one builder lacked pytest-asyncio and failed 148 tests."""
    if given or os.environ.get("REPACTED_PYTHON"):
        return given or os.environ["REPACTED_PYTHON"]
    for root in dict.fromkeys(r for r in (REPO, main_checkout()) if r):
        venv = root / VENV_PYTHON
        if os.access(venv, os.X_OK):
            return str(venv)
    return "python3"




def account_home() -> str:
    """The account's home from the password database, never $HOME (a builder's is a scratch dir)."""
    return pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir


def user_base(python: str) -> str | None:
    """Where `python` keeps its user site under the account's home (site.getuserbase()), or None
    when it cannot be asked. The scratch HOME moves that directory, and with it a user-installed
    pytest: the run then printed NO TEST COUNT."""
    env = {**os.environ, "HOME": account_home()}
    try:
        out = subprocess.run([python, "-c", "import site; print(site.getuserbase())"], env=env,
                             capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):
        return None
    return out.stdout.strip() or None if out.returncode == 0 else None


def live_runs_dir() -> str | None:
    """The run ledger's directory as the run-ledger hook resolves it (_repact_common.ledger_path,
    under the caller's environment), when this is a Claude Code session; else None."""
    if not os.environ.get(SESSION_ENV):
        return None
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, str(PLUGIN / "bin"))
        from _repact_common import ledger_path

        return str(ledger_path().parent)
    except Exception:   # noqa: BLE001 - the suite still runs; its log stays in the scratch data dir
        return None


def child_env(home: Path, python: str = "python3", through_tcount: bool = True) -> dict[str, str]:
    env = dict(os.environ)
    # Resolved before the scratch HOME is set. A --raw command is not run through tcount, so it
    # would hand the variable to whatever it runs.
    runs_dir = live_runs_dir() if through_tcount and not env.get("CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA") else None
    for key in ("CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR", "CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT"):
        env.pop(key, None)
    env["PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE"] = "1"
    if not env.get("PYTHONUSERBASE"):
        base = user_base(python)
        if base:
            env["PYTHONUSERBASE"] = base
    # huggingface_hub keeps the embedding model under $HOME/.cache/huggingface, so the scratch HOME
    # would hide it and the requires_embedding_backend tests would fail offline: keep the account's
    # cache unless the caller named one.
    if not (env.get("HF_HOME") or env.get("HF_HUB_CACHE")):
        env["HF_HOME"] = str(Path(env.get("XDG_CACHE_HOME") or Path(account_home()) / ".cache")
                             / "huggingface")
    env["HOME"] = str(home)
    # The core purity gate (tests/contract/test_core_purity.py) fails closed without the scrub
    # denylist, so every suite is told where the real one lives; it only reads it.
    source = denylist_dir()
    if DENYLIST_REQUIRED or any((source / name).is_file() for name in DENYLISTS):
        env["REPACT_PURITY_DENYLIST_DIR"] = str(source)
    else:
        env["REPACT_PURITY_NO_DENYLIST"] = "1"
    # tcount's log and run-ledger record must outlive a temp HOME, and must never land in the live one.
    env.setdefault("CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA", str(Path(tempfile.gettempdir()) / "repacted-test-runs"))
    if runs_dir:
        env[LOG_DIR_ENV] = runs_dir     # tcount's own log only; tcount does not pass it on
    return env


class Runner:
    """Runs each step (no inherited lock fds) in its own process group, forwarding HUP/INT/TERM to
    the WHOLE group: a signal that reached only tcount would orphan pytest, which would then keep
    running after this wrapper released the slot. After a signal no further step starts."""

    def __init__(self) -> None:
        self.proc: subprocess.Popen | None = None
        self.signalled: int | None = None
        self.last_log: str | None = None     # tcount's `log: <path>` line of the last captured step
        for sig in (signal.SIGHUP, signal.SIGINT, signal.SIGTERM):
            signal.signal(sig, self.forward)

    def forward(self, signum, _frame) -> None:
        self.signalled = signum
        if self.proc is not None:
            try:
                os.killpg(self.proc.pid, signum)
            except ProcessLookupError:
                pass

    def run(self, cmd: list[str], cwd: Path, env: dict[str, str],
            capture: bool) -> tuple[int, str, list[str]]:
        """(exit code, the tcount counts line, the failing ids tcount listed), the last two only
        when capture is set. A captured stdout is still echoed line by line as it arrives."""
        self.proc = subprocess.Popen(cmd, cwd=cwd, env=env, close_fds=True, start_new_session=True,
                                     stdout=subprocess.PIPE if capture else None,
                                     text=True if capture else None)
        if self.signalled is not None:  # a signal landed between steps, before this one started
            self.forward(self.signalled, None)
        counts, failing = "", []
        self.last_log = None
        if capture:
            for line in self.proc.stdout:
                sys.stdout.write(line)
                sys.stdout.flush()
                if line.startswith(COUNTS_PREFIX) and not counts:
                    counts = line.strip()
                elif line.startswith("FAILED "):
                    failing.append(line[len("FAILED "):].strip())
                elif line.startswith("log: "):
                    self.last_log = line[len("log: "):].strip()
        return self.proc.wait(), counts, failing


def load_baseline(path: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, set[str]], list[str]]:
    """{suite: known failing node ids} from `<suite> <node id> # <reason>` lines, and problems.
    A missing file, an unknown suite or an entry without a reason is a problem: fail closed."""
    known: dict[str, set[str]] = {suite: set() for suite in SUITES}
    if not path.is_file():
        return known, [f"no known-failures baseline at {path}"]
    problems = []
    for n, line in enumerate(path.read_text(encoding="utf-8").splitlines(), 1):
        if not line.strip() or line.lstrip().startswith("#"):
            continue
        head, _, reason = line.partition(" # ")
        suite, _, node = head.strip().partition(" ")
        if suite not in known or not node.strip() or not reason.strip():
            problems.append(f"baseline line {n} is not '<suite> <node id> # <reason>': {line!r}")
            continue
        known[suite].add(node.strip())
    return known, problems


def gate_verdict(results: list[tuple[str, int, str, list[str]]],
                 known: dict[str, set[str]], problems: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Verdict lines. The gate passes only when every suite's failing ids EQUAL its known set:
    a new failure fails it, and so does a known one that now passes or is gone (drift)."""
    problems = list(problems)
    new, drift, known_seen = [], [], 0
    for label, code, counts, failing in results:
        match = COUNTS_LINE.match(counts)
        if not match:
            problems.append(f"{label}: no count line (exit {code})")
            continue
        collected, failed = int(match.group(1)), int(match.group(2)) + int(match.group(3))
        observed = set(failing)
        if collected == 0:
            problems.append(f"{label}: no tests ran")
        if failed > len(observed):
            problems.append(f"{label}: {failed} failures but {len(observed)} listed; "
                            f"{failed - len(observed)} not listed, so the baseline cannot be compared")
        elif code != 0 and failed == 0:
            problems.append(f"{label}: exit {code} with no failing test")
        new += [f"{label} {node}" for node in sorted(observed - known[label])]
        drift += [f"{label} {node}" for node in sorted(known[label] - observed)]
        known_seen += len(observed & known[label])
    if not (new or drift or problems):
        return [f"run-tests: gate passed ({known_seen} known)"]
    lines = ["run-tests: gate FAILED"]
    if new:
        lines.append(f"run-tests: gate NEW failures: {', '.join(new)}")
    if drift:
        lines.append(f"run-tests: gate baseline drift (a known failure now passes or is gone): "
                     f"{', '.join(drift)}")
    lines += [f"run-tests: gate {problem}" for problem in problems]
    return lines


def denylist_dir() -> Path:
    """Where the real scrub denylists live: the account's home, never $HOME (a scratch HOME may
    already be in force). REPACTED_DENYLIST_DIR overrides it (tests of this wrapper only)."""
    override = os.environ.get("REPACTED_DENYLIST_DIR")
    return Path(override) if override else Path(pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_dir) / ".config" / "repacted"




def slowest_files(lines, top: int = SLOWEST_FILES) -> list[list]:
    """[[file, seconds], ...]: the `top` test files with the most wall in pytest's durations block
    (every setup, call and teardown line it lists, summed per file), slowest first; [] when the
    output holds no block. The file is the node id up to its first `::`."""
    walls: dict[str, float] = {}
    inside = False
    for line in lines:
        line = line.rstrip("\n")
        if SLOWEST_HEADER.match(line):
            inside = True
        elif inside and line.startswith("="):
            break
        elif inside and (match := DURATION_LINE.match(line.strip())):
            file = match.group(2).split("::", 1)[0]
            walls[file] = walls.get(file, 0.0) + float(match.group(1))
    ranked = sorted(walls.items(), key=lambda item: (-item[1], item[0]))[:top]
    return [[file, round(seconds, 2)] for file, seconds in ranked]


def log_slowest(log_path: str | None) -> list[list]:
    """slowest_files of a tcount log; [] when there is no log or it cannot be read."""
    if not log_path:
        return []
    try:
        with open(log_path, encoding="utf-8", errors="replace") as handle:
            return slowest_files(handle)
    except OSError:
        return []


def print_slowest(label: str, slowest: list[list]) -> None:
    if slowest:
        print(f"run-tests: {label:<10} slowest {len(slowest)} test files (s, setup+call+teardown over 0.1 s)")
        for file, seconds in slowest:
            print(f"  {seconds:8.2f}  {file}")


def publish_run(log_path: str | None, env: dict[str, str], slowest: list[list] | None = None) -> None:
    """Copy tcount's row for one suite run from the child's ledger (the scratch data dir) to the
    caller's live run ledger, so a HANDOFF that cites the run's counts or log resolves (e1baab9f:
    full-gate counts read as MISMATCH because only $TMPDIR/repacted-test-runs held them). Only
    this parent writes the live ledger; the child keeps its scratch HOME and data dir. The
    run-ledger hook attributes the row to the agent by its log path. A --full run's slowest
    files go into the copied row as `slowest`. Never fails the run."""
    if not log_path:
        return
    try:
        sys.path.insert(0, str(PLUGIN / "bin"))
        from _repact_common import LEDGER_FIELDS, ledger_append, ledger_path, read_ledger

        child = Path(env["CLAUDE_PLUGIN_DATA"]).expanduser() / "runs" / "ledger.jsonl"
        live = ledger_path()
        if child.resolve() == live.resolve():
            return
        rows = [row for row in read_ledger(child) if row.get("source") == "tcount" and row.get("log_path") == log_path]
        if rows:
            row = {key: rows[-1].get(key) for key in LEDGER_FIELDS}
            if slowest:
                row["slowest"] = slowest
            ledger_append(row, live)
    except Exception as exc:   # noqa: BLE001 - the suite's result stands whatever happens here
        print(f"run-tests: run not copied to the live ledger ({type(exc).__name__})", file=sys.stderr)


def run_steps(steps: list[tuple[str, list[str], Path]], env: dict[str, str], home: Path,
              gate: bool = True, verdict: bool = False) -> int:
    """Run the steps; with verdict (the merge gate) the result is read against the baseline."""
    runner = Runner()
    if len(steps) == 1 and not verdict:
        label, cmd, cwd = steps[0]
        code = runner.run(cmd, cwd, env, capture=True)[0]
        slowest = log_slowest(runner.last_log) if gate else []
        print_slowest(label, slowest)
        publish_run(runner.last_log, env, slowest)
        return code
    results: list[tuple[str, int, str, list[str]]] = []
    slowest_of: dict[str, list[list]] = {}
    for label, cmd, cwd in steps:
        if runner.signalled is not None:
            break
        print(f"run-tests: [{label}] {cwd}", file=sys.stderr, flush=True)
        links: list[Path] = []
        step_env = env
        try:
            code, counts, failing = runner.run(cmd, cwd, step_env, capture=True)
        finally:
            for link in links:
                link.unlink(missing_ok=True)
        slowest_of[label] = log_slowest(runner.last_log) if gate else []
        publish_run(runner.last_log, env, slowest_of[label])
        results.append((label, code, counts, failing))
    for label, code, counts, _ in results:
        print(f"run-tests: {label:<10} {counts or f'NO COUNT LINE (exit {code})'}")
    for label, _, _, _ in results:
        print_slowest(label, slowest_of[label])
    skipped = [label for label, _, _ in steps[len(results):]]
    if skipped:
        print(f"run-tests: stopped by signal {runner.signalled}; not run: {', '.join(skipped)}")
        codes = [code for _, code, _, _ in results if code != 0]
        return codes[0] if codes else 128 + (runner.signalled or 0)
    if not gate:                    # QUICK: counts only; the baseline verdict is the --full gate's
        codes = [code for _, code, _, _ in results if code != 0]
        return codes[0] if codes else 0
    baseline_path = Path(os.environ.get("REPACTED_KNOWN_FAILURES") or KNOWN_FAILURES)
    known, problems = load_baseline(baseline_path)
    lines = gate_verdict(results, known, problems)
    for line in lines:
        print(line)
    if lines[0].startswith("run-tests: gate passed"):
        return 0
    codes = [code for _, code, _, _ in results if code != 0]
    return codes[0] if codes else 1


def parse(argv: list[str]):
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="run-tests", add_help=True,
                                     formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter,
                                     epilog=__doc__.split("Examples", 1)[1].join(["Examples", ""]))
    parser.add_argument("--full", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--raw", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--status", action="store_true")
    parser.add_argument("--pkg")
    parser.add_argument("--home")
    parser.add_argument("--python")
    parser.add_argument("--wait", type=float, default=3600.0)
    if "--" in argv:
        cut = argv.index("--")
        own, rest = argv[:cut], argv[cut + 1:]
    else:
        own, rest = argv, []
    args, extra = parser.parse_known_args(own)
    return args, extra + rest


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    try:
        args, pytest_args = parse(argv)
        if args.status:
            return status()
        if args.full and args.raw:
            raise Usage("--full and --raw are exclusive")
        steps = build_steps(args, pytest_args)
        if args.full and pytest_args:
            print("run-tests: narrowed --full: only the named tests run (not the merge gate)", file=sys.stderr)
    except Usage as exc:
        print(f"run-tests: {exc}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_USAGE

    pkg = args.pkg or current_branch()
    deadline = time.monotonic() + args.wait
    held: list[int] = []
    sidecars: list[Path] = []
    ticket: Path | None = None
    try:
        if args.full:
            got = acquire_suite(pkg, deadline)
            if got is None:
                print(f"run-tests: suite slot not acquired within {args.wait:.0f}s; see --status. "
                      "Report it; do not bypass the lock.", file=sys.stderr)
                return EXIT_LOCK_TIMEOUT
            held.append(got[0])
            ticket = got[2]
            sidecars.append(write_owner(got[1], pkg))
        got = acquire(tuple(lock_dir() / name for name in WORKER_LOCKS), deadline)
        if got is None:
            print(f"run-tests: no worker slot free within {args.wait:.0f}s; see --status. "
                  "Report it; do not bypass the lock.", file=sys.stderr)
            return EXIT_LOCK_TIMEOUT
        held.append(got[0])
        sidecars.append(write_owner(got[1], pkg))
        print(f"run-tests: {pkg} holds {', '.join(p.name[:-len('.owner')] for p in sidecars)}",
              file=sys.stderr)

        scratch = Path(args.home) if args.home else Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="repacted-home."))
        try:
            python = default_python(args.python)
            return run_steps(steps, child_env(scratch, python, not args.raw), scratch, gate=args.full,
                             verdict=args.full and not pytest_args)
        finally:
            if not args.home:
                shutil.rmtree(scratch, ignore_errors=True)
    finally:
        for path in [*sidecars, *([ticket] if ticket else [])]:
            try:
                path.unlink()
            except OSError:
                pass
        for fd in held:
            os.close(fd)


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
